WEBVTT

00:00:00.105 --> 00:00:02.895
Serial and serializable sound almost the

00:00:02.908 --> 00:00:05.224
same, but the slides define them

00:00:05.237 --> 00:00:05.895
separately.

00:00:06.316 --> 00:00:07.737
Let's look at each definition.

00:00:08.578 --> 00:00:10.881
A serial schedule is defined by how the

00:00:10.999 --> 00:00:13.499
actions of each transaction are laid out.

00:00:13.907 --> 00:00:16.618
A serializable schedule is defined by the

00:00:16.631 --> 00:00:18.986
database state it leaves behind compared

00:00:18.986 --> 00:00:20.118
with a serial schedule.

00:00:20.954 --> 00:00:24.152
Here is schedule S3 from the slides.

00:00:24.652 --> 00:00:26.902
The slides note that switching the two

00:00:26.902 --> 00:00:31.494
reads on the same object, r2(x) and r1(x),

00:00:31.783 --> 00:00:33.862
gives another schedule, S4.

00:00:34.683 --> 00:00:38.039
This is S4, which the slides label serial.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:41.210
They state that S3 is view-equivalent to

00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:44.841
serial schedule S4, so S3 is

00:00:44.854 --> 00:00:45.986
view-serializable.

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:48.486
Now go back and try a new question

00:00:48.486 --> 00:00:49.078
yourself.
